<title>POLAND: BROKERAGES MERGER CLEARED.</title>
<headline>BROKERAGES MERGER CLEARED.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish anti-monopoly office has agreed for a planned merger of Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych SA's (BIG) and Bank Gdanski's brokerages, Gdanski said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Earlier the banks said that under the merger agreement BIG's broking subsidiary Dom Maklerski BIG Sp z o.o. would incorporate Gdanski's securities unit and take over its clients.</p>
<p>Early last month BIG became a majority owner of Bank Gdanski after it doubled its stake to about 63 percent, buying shares from state treasury. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
